Threat Hunt — Persistence via New Service Installation
Hypothesis
A threat actor who has already gained administrative privileges is attempting to establish persistence or perform lateral movement
. The hypothesis is that the actor is using tools like PsExec or custom scripts to install a new system service that will survive a reboot
.
Data Source
Windows System Log: Event ID 7045 (A new service was installed)
.
Sysmon: Event ID 13 (Registry value set) to monitor changes to the Services registry hive
.
KQL (Microsoft Sentinel/Defender)
// Detect new services with suspicious names or paths
DeviceEvents
| where ActionType == "ServiceInstalled"
| where ServiceName matches regex @"^[a-zA-Z0-9]{8}$" or ServiceFileName contains "Temp"
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, ServiceName, ServiceFileName, ServiceType
Logic: Targets services with randomly generated names (common in Impacket/PsExec) or those running from temporary directories
.
SPL (Splunk)
index=system EventCode=7045 
| eval is_psexec=if(match(Service_Name,"psexesvc"),"Yes","No")
| table _time, host, Service_Name, Service_File_Name, is_psexec
Logic: Specifically identifies the installation of the PsExec service, a classic tool for remote command execution and lateral movement
.
Findings
The hunt identified a new service named B6X9Z2R1 installed on a file server
. The Service_File_Name pointed to a binary in C:\Windows\Temp, confirming an unauthorized lateral movement attempt using the Impacket framework
.
False Positives
Software Updates: Legitimate applications or drivers that install temporary services during a patch
.
IT Administration: Authorized use of PsExec by the IT team for remote troubleshooting
.
MITRE ATT&CK
Tactic: Persistence (TA0003) / Lateral Movement (TA0008)
.
Technique: Create or Modify System Process: System Service (T1543.003)
.
Detection Improvement
Service Monitoring: Alert on any service creation where the AccountName is not a standard system account (e.g., LocalSystem)
.
Privileged Access: Restrict administrative permissions on endpoints to prevent unauthorized service installation
.
